  "summary": "Four documents directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling (Bayesian hierarchical models) to hate speech detection. [V0113] (Adebayo et al., 2026) evaluates on ToxiBench, reporting AUROC 0.67. [V0114] (Brennan et al., 2018) evaluates on GridWatch, reporting F1=0.74. [V0115] (Chen et al., 2019) evaluates on ProtMap, reporting accuracy 0.81. [V0116] (Duarte et al., 2020) evaluates on FireScope, reporting MAE 0.88. A fifth slot is filled by [V0034], which only mentions the method-topic combination as prior work and does not itself apply it, making it the weakest inclusion. Documents such as [V0107], [V0108], [V0105] address hate speech but use decentralised training rather than Bayesian hierarchical models, and are therefore not directly relevant to the research question.",
